.Dd June 27, 2026
.Dt CAP_XFER_CAPMODE 2
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm cap_xfer_capmode
.Nd restrict descriptor transfer to capability-mode connections
.Sh LIBRARY
.Lb libc
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.In sys/capsicum.h
.Ft int
.Fn cap_xfer_capmode "int fd"
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The
.Fn cap_xfer_capmode
system call sets a monotonic per-descriptor flag that restricts how the
descriptor may be transferred via
.Xr sendmsg 2
with an
.Dv SCM_RIGHTS
control message.
Once set, the descriptor may only be sent over a
.Ux Ns -domain
socket that has the
.Dv LOCAL_CAP_SOCKET
attribute
.Pq see Xr unix 4 ,
meaning both endpoints were created in capability mode.
If the sending socket lacks
.Dv LOCAL_CAP_SOCKET ,
.Xr sendmsg 2
fails with
.Er ENOTCAPABLE
and the descriptor is not delivered.
.Pp
The flag is monotonic: once set it cannot be cleared.
Calling
.Fn cap_xfer_capmode
on a descriptor that already has the flag set is permitted and has no
effect.
.Pp
This system call controls
.Em which connections
may be used to transfer the descriptor.
It is orthogonal to
.Xr cap_xfer_limit 2 ,
which controls
.Em how many times
the descriptor may be transferred, and may be combined with it freely.
.Pp
.Sy Flag propagation:
when a process successfully receives the descriptor, the new descriptor
installed in the receiver's file descriptor table inherits the flag.
Subsequent transfers of the received descriptor are therefore also
restricted to sockets with
.Dv LOCAL_CAP_SOCKET .
The flag cannot be cleared by the receiving process.
.Pp
This system call is allowed in capability mode
.Pq see Xr cap_enter 2 .
.Sh SECURITY CONSIDERATIONS
Combined with
.Xr cap_xfer_limit 2
.Pq Dv CAP_XFER_ONCE ,
.Xr cap_cloexec_limit 2
.Pq Dv CAP_CLOEXEC_LOCKED ,
and
.Xr cap_clofork_limit 2
.Pq Dv CAP_CLOFORK_LOCKED ,
.Fn cap_xfer_capmode
creates a closed security boundary: the descriptor can be transferred
exactly once, only over a connection where both endpoints are in
capability mode, and will be closed on exec or fork in the receiving
process.
This pattern is appropriate when delegating a sensitive resource to a
sandboxed worker that must not be able to exfiltrate it further.
.Pp
Descriptors marked with the
.Dv UF_CAP_SUFFICIENT
flag
.Pq set via Xr socketpair 2 with Dv SOCK_CAPMODE or directly
bypass ambient authority checks when used by a capability-mode process,
providing capability-sufficient access without requiring additional
ambient authority.
.Sh RETURN VALUES
.Rv -std
.Sh ERRORS
.Fn cap_xfer_capmode
succeeds unless:
.Bl -tag -width Er
.It Bq Er EBADF
The
.Fa fd
argument is not a valid active descriptor.
.It Bq Er ENOSYS
The running kernel was compiled without
.Cd "options CAPABILITIES" .
.El
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr cap_clofork_limit 2 ,
.Xr cap_cloexec_limit 2 ,
.Xr cap_enter 2 ,
.Xr cap_rights_limit 2 ,
.Xr cap_xfer_limit 2 ,
.Xr sendmsg 2 ,
.Xr socketpair 2 ,
.Xr capsicum 4 ,
.Xr unix 4
.Sh HISTORY
The
.Fn cap_xfer_capmode
system call first appeared in
.Fx 16.0 .
